---
/**
 * Book I, Ch. X, Prop. 1: an LSTM cell. The carry line runs straight through
 * with only a multiplication and an addition on it, which is the point: the
 * gradient has a road home that does not pass through a weight matrix.
 */
---
<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 720 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="gt-t gt-d" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" style="--fig-min: 640px">
  <title id="gt-t">An LSTM cell and its uninterrupted carry line</title>
  <desc id="gt-d">
    A horizontal line across the top carries the cell state from left to right,
    crossed only by one multiplication, by the forget gate, and one addition,
    of the candidate scaled by the input gate. A branch from the line passes
    through tanh and is multiplied by the output gate to give the hidden state.
    All three gates and the candidate read the preceding hidden state and the
    current input.
  </desc>

  <text x="0" y="22" class="t-lab">the carry line</text>

  <line x1="20" y1="70" x2="700" y2="70" class="s3" stroke-width="2" />
  <text x="20" y="58" class="t-key">c(t−1)</text>
  <text x="700" y="58" class="t-key" text-anchor="end">c(t)</text>

  <circle cx="200" cy="70" r="14" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="200" y="76" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">×</text>
  <circle cx="400" cy="70" r="14" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="400" y="76" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">+</text>

  <rect x="130" y="200" width="140" height="48" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="200" y="221" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">forget gate f</text>
  <text x="200" y="239" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">σ → (0, 1)</text>
  <line x1="200" y1="198" x2="200" y2="96" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="195,96 200,84 205,96" class="head" />

  <circle cx="400" cy="140" r="14" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="400" y="146" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">×</text>
  <line x1="400" y1="126" x2="400" y2="96" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="395,96 400,84 405,96" class="head" />

  <rect x="285" y="200" width="110" height="48" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="340" y="221" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">input gate i</text>
  <text x="340" y="239" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">σ → (0, 1)</text>
  <line x1="350" y1="198" x2="390" y2="151" class="wire" />

  <rect x="410" y="200" width="110" height="48" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="465" y="221" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">candidate c̃</text>
  <text x="465" y="239" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">tanh → (−1, 1)</text>
  <line x1="455" y1="198" x2="410" y2="151" class="wire" />

  <line x1="560" y1="70" x2="560" y2="118" class="wire" />
  <rect x="525" y="118" width="70" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="560" y="137" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">tanh</text>
  <line x1="560" y1="146" x2="560" y2="166" class="wire" />
  <circle cx="560" cy="180" r="14" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="560" y="186" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">×</text>
  <line x1="574" y1="180" x2="692" y2="180" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="692,175 704,180 692,185" class="head" />
  <text x="700" y="168" class="t-key" text-anchor="end">h(t)</text>

  <rect x="585" y="200" width="115" height="48" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="642" y="221" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">output gate o</text>
  <text x="642" y="239" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">σ → (0, 1)</text>
  <line x1="610" y1="198" x2="570" y2="191" class="wire" />

  <line x1="20" y1="280" x2="700" y2="280" class="wire-soft" />
  {[200, 340, 465, 642].map((cx) => (
    <line x1={cx} y1="280" x2={cx} y2="250" class="wire-soft" />
  ))}
  <text x="20" y="298" class="t-sm">h(t−1), x(t): every gate and the candidate read the same two vectors</text>

  <text x="0" y="324" class="t-sm">Holding the gates fixed, the carry line's derivative is diag(f). No weight matrix stands on it.</text>
</svg>
